WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:14.394
Edmund and Goneril rode up to her castle and were met by Oswald.

2
00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:17.336
"Madam, I must warn you," he said.

3
00:00:17.356 --> 00:00:19.537
"Your husband takes the king's side.

4
00:00:20.057 --> 00:00:21.498
He does not want to fight the French."

5
00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:25.080
"He is a weakling," Goneril fumed.

6
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.381
She smiled invitingly at Edmund.

7
00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:30.563
"Not like you, fair Edmund."

8
00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.124
She kissed him on the forehead.

9
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.881
"Now, return to my sister and Cornwall.

10
00:00:36.382 --> 00:00:37.923
I will soon send word to you."

11
00:00:39.223 --> 00:00:43.365
After Edmund rode away, the gates opened and the Duke of Albany strode out.

12
00:00:43.385 --> 00:00:48.228
"Goneril," he cried, "what have you and your sister done to your father?

13
00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:50.429
You are tigers, not daughters!"

14
00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.071
"Silence, you coward!"

15
00:00:53.591 --> 00:00:54.431
Goneril retorted.

16
00:00:54.451 --> 00:00:58.333
"Cordelia and the French army are at Dover—we are at war!"

17
00:00:58.353 --> 00:01:04.477
"If the French have invaded British soil, then I must fight," said Albany unhappily.

18
00:01:06.018 --> 00:01:08.140
They were interrupted by a messenger on horseback.

19
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.961
"The Duke of Cornwall is dead!"

20
00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:10.782
he shouted.

21
00:01:11.903 --> 00:01:15.546
"Slain by a servant who tried to stop him from putting out Gloucester's eyes!"

22
00:01:15.566 --> 00:01:18.268
"Where was Edmund when this was happening?"

23
00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:19.449
asked Albany.

24
00:01:19.469 --> 00:01:21.210
"Gone, sir.

25
00:01:21.751 --> 00:01:23.953
It was he who informed against his father."

26
00:01:23.973 --> 00:01:25.934
"Cornwall is dead?"

27
00:01:26.455 --> 00:01:27.055
thought Goneril.

28
00:01:27.075 --> 00:01:29.457
"Then my sister is free to remarry.

29
00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:31.499
And she will soon see my Edmund.

30
00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:32.780
I don't like this."

31
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.461
Goneril quickly formed a plan.

32
00:01:35.981 --> 00:01:37.562
She went inside and wrote a letter.

33
00:01:38.663 --> 00:01:41.104
"Take this to Edmund," she commanded Oswald.

34
00:01:41.564 --> 00:01:43.605
"And if you see Gloucester, kill him.

35
00:01:44.746 --> 00:01:47.587
He stirs up too much sympathy and makes us look bad.

36
00:01:48.088 --> 00:01:49.388
We will meet you in Dover."

37
00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:57.433
Edgar and Gloucester were nearing Dover when they encountered Lear, dressed in strange clothing, with wildflowers in his

38
00:01:57.493 --> 00:01:58.593
hair and around his neck.

39
00:02:00.134 --> 00:02:01.315
"I am the king himself!"

40
00:02:01.975 --> 00:02:02.535
Lear babbled.

41
00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:03.908
"Look, a mouse!

42
00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:07.892
They flattered me like a dog "I know that voice!"

43
00:02:08.372 --> 00:02:09.173
exclaimed Gloucester.

44
00:02:09.193 --> 00:02:11.615
"My lord, do you know who I am?"

45
00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:14.938
Lear stared at Gloucester's empty eye sockets.

46
00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:17.560
At last, he said, "You are Gloucester."

47
00:02:18.761 --> 00:02:21.323
At that moment, Cordelia's servants arrived.

48
00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:26.287
"The queen of France wants us to bring her father to her," one said, and they led the

49
00:02:26.307 --> 00:02:26.808
king away.

50
00:02:28.029 --> 00:02:30.310
Then Edgar saw Oswald approaching.

51
00:02:32.456 --> 00:02:33.617
"Traitor, you must die!"

52
00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:36.778
Oswald shouted at Gloucester, his hand on his sword.

53
00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:41.720
Moving quickly, Edgar drew his knife and stabbed Oswald in the chest.

54
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:49.203
Oswald fell and whispered, "Take my purse and deliver the letter inside to Edmund, Earl of Gloucester.

55
00:02:49.923 --> 00:02:54.485
I am dying Edgar's eyes widened as he read the letter.

56
00:02:54.505 --> 00:02:56.246
"I must warn Albany!

57
00:02:56.746 --> 00:02:58.927
Goneril wants Edmund to kill her husband.

58
00:02:59.427 --> 00:03:00.648
Then she will marry Edmund."

59
00:03:02.228 --> 00:03:06.171
At the French camp, Cordelia's doctors had given Lear a potion to calm him.

60
00:03:06.711 --> 00:03:09.053
He lay sleeping as Cordelia watched over him.

61
00:03:10.314 --> 00:03:12.375
At last, Lear opened his eyes.

62
00:03:12.395 --> 00:03:14.757
"Am I in my right mind?"

63
00:03:15.077 --> 00:03:15.517
he murmured.

64
00:03:15.537 --> 00:03:17.599
"Are you my child Cordelia?"

65
00:03:17.619 --> 00:03:22.502
"I am," she said, weeping and tenderly taking his hand.

66
00:03:22.522 --> 00:03:25.764
"I am very foolish," said Lear.

67
00:03:25.784 --> 00:03:27.766
"I must ask your forgiveness."

68
00:03:29.046 --> 00:03:35.033
Meanwhile, at the British camp in Dover, Regan had asked Edmund to lead her army, since Cornwall was

69
00:03:35.073 --> 00:03:40.396
dead. "I wish to marry you," Regan said, "but are you in love with Goneril?"

70
00:03:40.416 --> 00:03:43.697
"By my honor, no," answered Edmund.

71
00:03:44.197 --> 00:03:46.978
To himself, he said, "Both sisters want me.

72
00:03:47.499 --> 00:03:48.819
I'll turn this to my advantage!"

73
00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:56.322
In another part of the camp, Edgar, now disguised as a peasant, approached Albany and handed him the

74
00:03:56.362 --> 00:03:58.043
letter he'd taken from Oswald.

75
00:03:58.063 --> 00:04:01.576
"Your life is in danger," Edgar said.

76
00:04:01.596 --> 00:04:06.858
"If you win the battle, sound your trumpets and a knight will come to prove what this letter

77
00:04:06.898 --> 00:04:10.460
contains." The battle began early the next morning.

78
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.381
It was short and bloody, and the French forces were defeated.

79
00:04:15.582 --> 00:04:18.723
Lear and Cordelia were captured and brought to the British camp.

80
00:04:18.743 --> 00:04:23.685
"Take them to the prison," Edmund ordered an army captain and handed him a note.

81
00:04:24.225 --> 00:04:26.727
"Follow these instructions, and you will be rewarded."

82
00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.969
As the captain led Cordelia and the king away, Cordelia was heartbroken.

83
00:04:33.089 --> 00:04:38.551
But her father tried to comfort her, saying, "In prison, we'll be like two birds in a cage.

84
00:04:39.132 --> 00:04:42.333
We'll sing and pray and laugh and tell old tales."

85
00:04:43.593 --> 00:04:47.315
When Albany heard Lear and Cordelia were in prison, he was furious.

86
00:04:47.335 --> 00:04:51.837
"Edmund," he said, "that decision was not yours to make.

87
00:04:52.337 --> 00:04:53.758
You are not my equal in rank."

88
00:04:54.938 --> 00:04:56.859
"He led my army," Regan interrupted.

89
00:04:56.879 --> 00:04:59.560
"I declare him my lord and master."

90
00:05:01.108 --> 00:05:02.969
Jealous, Goneril jumped in.

91
00:05:02.989 --> 00:05:04.270
"Will you marry him?"

92
00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.051
"Not so fast," said Albany.

93
00:05:07.071 --> 00:05:10.813
"I arrest you for treason, Edmund, and Goneril too.

94
00:05:11.394 --> 00:05:13.495
You planned to kill me and get married!"

95
00:05:14.715 --> 00:05:16.897
"You have no proof," Goneril shot back.

96
00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.338
Regan looked pale and weak.

97
00:05:19.358 --> 00:05:21.699
"I am not well," she whispered.

98
00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.360
Two servants led her away.

99
00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:27.382
"I will defend my honor," Edmund declared.

100
00:05:27.402 --> 00:05:28.643
"Who challenges me?"

101
00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:34.457
Suddenly, Edgar appeared in the armor of a knight, his face hidden by his helmet.

102
00:05:35.597 --> 00:05:42.239
"Edmund," he cried, "you are a traitor against your father, your brother, and the Duke of Albany!"

103
00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.380
The two men drew their swords and fought.

104
00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.181
Edgar finally struck Edmund down.

105
00:05:49.381 --> 00:05:50.441
Goneril ran to him.

106
00:05:50.461 --> 00:05:53.622
"Edmund," she shrieked, "are you badly hurt?"

107
00:05:55.203 --> 00:05:59.804
"Enough, Goneril," said Albany sternly and held out the letter she'd written to Edmund.

108
00:06:00.288 --> 00:06:02.130
"Here is proof of your wickedness!"

109
00:06:03.351 --> 00:06:04.151
"What do I care?"

110
00:06:04.612 --> 00:06:07.814
Goneril said haughtily, but there was a desperate look in her eyes.

111
00:06:08.395 --> 00:06:10.736
She rushed away to the tent she shared with her sister.

112
00:06:11.957 --> 00:06:15.540
Edgar removed his helmet and knelt beside Edmund, who struggled to breathe.

113
00:06:16.081 --> 00:06:17.882
Remorse washed over the dying man.

114
00:06:17.902 --> 00:06:23.687
"Brother," Edmund said, "I have done all you accuse me of, and more.

115
00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:30.921
May you and our father forgive me "Alas," Edgar said, "our father has died."

116
00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:35.044
Edgar related how he had disguised himself and then met up with Gloucester.

117
00:06:35.064 --> 00:06:39.788
"When I finally revealed myself to him this morning, he was overjoyed.

118
00:06:40.228 --> 00:06:41.990
But the shock stopped his poor heart."

119
00:06:43.531 --> 00:06:46.814
Just then a messenger ran toward them, carrying a bloody knife.

120
00:06:48.035 --> 00:06:51.037
"My lady Goneril is dead, by her own hand," he cried.

121
00:06:51.057 --> 00:06:54.821
"And she confessed to poisoning her sister, who is dead too!"

122
00:06:54.841 --> 00:06:57.343
"This is also my fault."

123
00:06:57.903 --> 00:06:58.704
gasped Edmund.

124
00:06:59.128 --> 00:07:00.449
"They both wanted to marry me.

125
00:07:00.929 --> 00:07:02.990
But maybe I can finally do some good.

126
00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:06.991
I secretly ordered Lear and Cordelia to be killed.

127
00:07:07.872 --> 00:07:10.713
Send someone to the prison to stop the executions!"

128
00:07:11.573 --> 00:07:13.414
Edmund said, right before he died.

129
00:07:14.314 --> 00:07:15.095
But it was too late.

130
00:07:15.615 --> 00:07:19.016
Within moments, Lear appeared, carrying Cordelia's body.

131
00:07:19.477 --> 00:07:21.377
The faithful Kent followed behind him.

132
00:07:22.758 --> 00:07:24.219
"She's gone forever!"

133
00:07:24.759 --> 00:07:25.359
wailed the king.

134
00:07:25.379 --> 00:07:27.340
"Curses on you murderers!"

135
00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:29.821
He looked up and saw Kent.

136
00:07:30.341 --> 00:07:31.182
"Are you not Kent?"

137
00:07:31.622 --> 00:07:32.883
he asked, confused.

138
00:07:34.104 --> 00:07:36.546
"Sir, I am," Kent replied.

139
00:07:36.566 --> 00:07:38.187
"I am also Caius.

140
00:07:38.787 --> 00:07:41.109
I chose to stay with you through all your trials."

141
00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.912
"Good Kent, you are welcome here," said Lear.

142
00:07:46.413 --> 00:07:47.894
He looked at his daughter's face again.

143
00:07:47.914 --> 00:07:56.260
"Oh, Cordelia, why should a dog, a horse, a rat have life, and you no breath at all?"

144
00:07:57.512 --> 00:08:00.074
The death of his innocent child was too much to bear.

145
00:08:00.615 --> 00:08:02.456
Lear plunged into madness again.

146
00:08:02.476 --> 00:08:06.760
"Look," he whispered, imagining she was still alive.

147
00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:14.926
"Her lips, they move Then Lear, his heart broken, took one final breath and fell to the ground.

148
00:08:16.087 --> 00:08:20.691
"He is gone," said Kent, gazing down at the master he had served so loyally.

149
00:08:20.711 --> 00:08:23.333
"It is a wonder he endured so long."

150
00:08:23.353 --> 00:08:27.941
"All is woe in the kingdom now," murmured Albany.

151
00:08:27.961 --> 00:08:31.625
"The oldest have suffered most," said Edgar.

152
00:08:31.645 --> 00:08:35.989
"Surely, we who are young will never see such misery again."
